========================================================================================
CBO-GAP Phase 11 — regime map, onset curve, diffusion energy
========================================================================================
  PRE-REGISTERED (fixed before the first run):
    RATE-CONSISTENT AT TOLERANCE 0.15 iff bootstrap 95% upper bound <= -0.85;
    counts also at [0.1, 0.15, 0.2] and with Bonferroni adjustment.
    Bootstrap unit: the independent coupled realization; the two-arm
    comparison resamples PAIRED on the shared realization index.
    EQUIVALENCE by two one-sided tests at margin 0.05, not by absence
    of significance. ONSET by free-breakpoint profile least squares;
    it differs from r = 1 only if the interval excludes 1.
    Measured noise floor from audit.py: 0.0219.

  DIFFUSION ENERGY, the referee's question answered:
    isotropic   trace of covariance = d sigma^2 |x-v|^2
    anisotropic trace of covariance =   sigma^2 |x-v|^2
    so matched sigma means the isotropic system injects d times the
    total quadratic variation, and matching the trace requires
    sigma_aniso = sqrt(d) sigma_iso, which is exactly matched r.
    Phase 9 called matched r the unfair comparison. The algebra says
    matched r is the matched-energy comparison. Both arms are
    legitimate; the realised trace is measured below either way.

