P11.2 — THE ONSET CURVE: does the degradation onset move with d?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Mean exponent at tau_0 = 0.1; free-breakpoint estimate with a
  bootstrap interval over objectives and realizations.

  isotropic
        d     r=1.0     r=2.0     r_onset              95% CI
       10    -1.003    -0.972       1.000         [1.00,1.00]
       40    -0.903    -0.414       1.000         [1.00,1.00]

  anisotropic
        d     r=1.0     r=2.0     r_onset              95% CI
       10    -1.038    -0.588       1.000         [1.00,1.00]
       40    -0.752    -0.552       1.000         [1.00,1.00]

  If r_onset is constant in d, the sufficient condition is the right
  normalisation and its boundary is merely conservative. If it falls
  with d, the condition is the wrong normalisation.

